# 16. Non-Functional Requirements

## NFR-001: Performance

MVP targets:

- Document extraction: under 90 seconds per document
- Classification: under 15 seconds after extraction
- Compliance check: under 10 seconds
- Packet generation: under 15 seconds
- Page load: under 2 seconds

Production targets:

- API response under 2 seconds for simple queries
- Batch processing 500 documents/hour

---

## NFR-002: Accuracy

Prototype targets:

- Header field extraction: 80%+
- Line item extraction: 70%+
- HS top-5: 70%+
- HS top-1: 50%+

Pilot targets:

- Header field extraction: 90%+
- Line item extraction: 80%+
- HS top-5: 85%+
- HS top-1: 70%+

Production targets:

- Header field extraction: 95%+
- Line item extraction: 90%+
- HS top-5: 92%+
- HS top-1: 80%+

---

## NFR-003: Availability

Prototype:

- Local Docker deployment

Production:

- 99.5% uptime initially
- 99.9% later

---

## NFR-004: Security

Required:

- TLS everywhere
- Encryption at rest
- Secure secrets
- API rate limiting
- Input validation
- SQL injection prevention
- XSS prevention
- CSRF protection
- File upload validation
- Tenant isolation
- Audit logs

---

## NFR-005: POPIA Compliance

Because South Africa applies POPIA:

- Personal information must be minimized.
- Contact details should be stored only where necessary.
- Provide data deletion workflow.
- Provide data export workflow.
- Maintain processing records.
- Have operator/processor agreements.
- Store data in South Africa where possible.
- If using foreign AI providers, disclose cross-border processing where required.

Important:

- Do not use customer documents to train public models without permission.
- Provide opt-in/opt-out for model improvement.

---

## NFR-006: Explainability

Every AI recommendation must include:

- Confidence score
- Reasoning
- Source reference
- Alternatives

Classification must not be a black box.

---

## NFR-007: Human-in-the-Loop

No AI output should be treated as final legal/customs advice.

High-risk decisions require human approval.

Product should display:

> AI-assisted recommendation. Final responsibility remains with the user/clearing agent.

---

## NFR-008: Observability

System must log:

- Request logs
- Job logs
- AI extraction logs
- Classification logs
- Error logs
- API usage
- Latency metrics
- Confidence metrics

Use:

- Structured JSON logs
- Correlation IDs
- Sentry or similar error tracking

---

## NFR-009: Scalability

Architecture must support:

- Multi-tenant SaaS
- Background workers
- Horizontal scaling
- Async jobs
- Object storage
- Vector search
- API gateway later

---

## NFR-010: Maintainability

